590 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (To translate our findings into actionable product insights, we segmented users based on their primary motivations for gameplay, rather than purely demographic characteristics. This approach allowed us to focus on why users engage, which is more directly tied to product experience and growth opportunities.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
591 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (From our survey data, two dominant and addressable segments emerged: users primarily motivated by entertainment and those motivated by perceived cognitive engagement \(e.g., improving memory, focus, or mental stimulation\). Notably, these segments represent a significant portion of the user base, with 33.7% of respondents identifying with entertainment-driven motivations and 30.8% with cognitively motivated drivers.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
592 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 321 0 R
/E (While additional motivations \(such as competition or relaxation\) were present, these two segments represented the most significant and strategically relevant groups in terms of both scale and potential impact.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
